          "notes": "Towards the middle of the 19th century scientists made a fundamental breakthrough In our understanding of how life works , They realised that the basic unit of life is the cell The origins of this idea go back to the early days of microscopy when an Engl lish scientist Robert Hooke decided t0 examine thin slices of plant material, He chose cork as one of his examples Looking down the microscope he made drawing t0 show the regular appearance of the structure, aS YOu can see in Figure 12, In 665 he published book containing this drawing",
