        {
          "blockId": "6a98745b5e7e8b0004fc3d4b",
          "contentValue": "A cell can be thought of as bag in which the chemistry of life occurs The activity going On inside the cell is therefore separated from the environment outside the cell  The bag Or cell, is surrounded by thin membrane The membrane  essential feature of all cells because it controls exchange between the cell and its environment It can act dS barrier, but it can also control movement of materials across the membrane in both directions The membrane therefore described as partially permeable If it were freely permeable, life could not exist, because the chemicals of the cell would simply mix with the surrounding chemicals by diflusion and the inside of the cell would be the same aS the outside",
          "contentType": "Paragraph",
          "coordinates": {
            "x": 50.59,
            "y": 22.59,
            "width": 39.5,
            "height": 21.06,
            "unit": "percentage"
