          "blockId": "6a9874541af52e00046b8b8c",
          "contentValue": "During the 2Uth century scientists studying the cells of bacteria and of more complex organisms such as plants and animals began t0 realise that there were two fundamentally diflerent kinds of cells Some cells were very simple but some were much larger and more complex The complex cells contained nucleus Apluralt nucleip surrounded by two membranes The genetie material, DNA was in the nucleus In the simple cells the DNA was not surrounded by membranes but apparently free in the cytoplasm",
