        {
          "blockId": "6a9874565e7e8b0004fc3d21",
          "contentValue": "are unfamiliar t0 most people Before studying light and electron microscopy further YOU need t0 become familiar with these units According to international agreement, the International System of Units SL units  should be used, In this system, the basic unit of length is the metre ksymbol, mj More units are created by going thousand times larger O smaller Standard prefixes are used for the units For example, the prefix  kilo means 1UOO times Thus kilometre LOUO metres The units of length relevant to cell studies are shown in Table L13 The smallest structure visible with the human eye is about 50-100 um in diameter  roughly the diameter of the sharp end of piny The cells in your body vary in size from about 4m to 40 um, It is difficult to imagine how small these cells are  especrally when they ure clearly visible using microscope An average bacterial cell is about Hm acrOSS One of the smallest structures yoU will study in this book is the ribosome, which is only about 25 nm in diameterl You could line up about 20 Ou0 ribosomes across the full stop at the end of this sentence",
          "contentType": "Paragraph",
