        {
          "blockId": "6a9874581af52e00046b8bba",
          "contentValue": "<p>showing the structure of generalised plant cell, both as seen with light microscope QA generalised cell shows all the structures that may commonly be found In cell 9 Figures and 17 are photomicrographs A photomicrograph is photograph of specimen as seen with light microscope Figure 16 shows some human cells Figure 17 shows plant cell taken from leaf Both figures show cells magnified 400 times, which is equivalent t0 using the high- power objective lens on light microscope See also Figures 8a and Sb for labelled drawings of these figures Many of the cell contents are colourless and transparent 50 they need t0 be stained with coloured dyes t0 be seen The human cells in Figure 1 6 have been stained The chromatin n the nuclei IS particularly heavily stained The plant cells in Figure 1,5 have not been stained because the chloroplasts contain the green pigment chlorophyll and are easily visible without staining</p>",
          "contentType": "Paragraph",
